import{_ as n,o as t,c as i,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 955 | Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules · Rule 21 | Never Retcon, Never End Unfinished","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 955 | Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules · Rule 21 | Never Retcon, Never End Unfinished","no":955,"module":5,"tags":["Heavenly-Dao Rule","Rule 21","No Retcon","No Unfinished End","Law-First Axiom"],"related":["20-Anchor Structure and Hierarchy","954-Law Comes First","956-Setting Self-Consistency Above Plot Convenience"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0955_模块5-规则二十一-永不吃书永不烂尾.md","filePath":"en/0955_模块5-规则二十一-永不吃书永不烂尾.md"}'),a={name:"en/0955_模块5-规则二十一-永不吃书永不烂尾.md"};function r(s,e,l,u,c,d){return t(),i("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="entry-955-anti-predation-heavenly-dao-rules-·-rule-21-never-retcon-never-end-unfinished" tabindex="-1">Entry 955 | Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules · Rule 21 | Never Retcon, Never End Unfinished <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-955-anti-predation-heavenly-dao-rules-·-rule-21-never-retcon-never-end-unfinished" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 955 | Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules · Rule 21 | Never Retcon, Never End Unfinished&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 5 · Civilization Final-Finalization Canonical Entries | Benchmark base: Document 20 | Series: Complete Collection of Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-the-cosmos-may-not-temporarily-change-settings-and-may-not-run-away-mid-writing" tabindex="-1">Introduction: the cosmos may not temporarily change settings, and may not run away mid-writing <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-the-cosmos-may-not-temporarily-change-settings-and-may-not-run-away-mid-writing" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: the cosmos may not temporarily change settings, and may not run away mid-writing&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The old cosmos&#39;s cultivation civilizations are essentially all &quot;stories that were written.&quot; Stories have stories&#39; fates — once the author gets carried away, he retcons: earlier it says some method is the world&#39;s first, later the protagonist crushes it underfoot; earlier it says some strong one is invincible, later to make way for a new villain, the old setting quietly expires. Writing to the end it cannot be patched, and it ends unfinished: the protagonist suddenly says &quot;I have awakened,&quot; the world suddenly &quot;just is,&quot; and Myriad Ranks&#39; causality is flung aside. Heavenly-Dao Rule 21 is civilizational finalization&#39;s final judgment on this matter: Heng Yuan Zhou this &quot;great book&quot; never retcons and never ends unfinished. Once a setting is anchored it is law-protected; once a worldview is opened it must be written to the closed loop.</p><p>The six top-level axioms converge here: the law-first axiom is this rule&#39;s body, directly requiring &quot;never retcon, never end unfinished&quot;; the anti-predation axiom ensures &quot;no retconning&quot; does not quietly launder old predation settings into new settings; the republican axiom of Myriad Races decides Myriad Ranks the readers have the right to see a complete closed-loop ending; the collective-ascension axiom requires the story&#39;s terminus be whole-system ascension, not an individual protagonist&#39;s ascension; the causal self-discipline axiom requires every setting change leave a trace for traceability; the law-first axiom&#39;s twin, Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law, gives &quot;no retconning&quot; its confidence — since everyone inherently possesses basic infinite power and predation loses meaning, the story need not manufacture conflict by temporarily inflating villains and temporarily suppressing protagonists, and naturally need not retcon.</p><h2 id="i-rule-content-three-iron-laws-of-no-retcon-no-unfinished-end" tabindex="-1">I. Rule Content: Three Iron Laws of No Retcon, No Unfinished End <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-rule-content-three-iron-laws-of-no-retcon-no-unfinished-end" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Rule Content: Three Iron Laws of No Retcon, No Unfinished End&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Anchored settings may not be unilaterally overturned</strong>: any setting written into the law library (realms, methods, causality, clan relations) may not be voided for plot convenience; genuine adjustments go through the law-amendment procedure (Entry 931);</li><li><strong>Conflict must be explained, not covered</strong>: when new and old settings appear in surface conflict, the Anchor Council must issue a legal interpretation explaining their unifying logic; &quot;author&#39;s-amnesia&quot; evasion is forbidden;</li><li><strong>The closed loop must be written to the end</strong>: once civilizational evolution is opened, it must be deduced to the hyper-multiverse&#39;s only complete civilizational closed loop; &quot;protagonist ascends and the story ends, Myriad Ranks&#39; fate left blank&quot; unfinished endings are forbidden.</li></ol><h2 id="ii-jurisprudential-basis" tabindex="-1">II. Jurisprudential Basis <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-jurisprudential-basis" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Jurisprudential Basis&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anchor-structure argument</strong>: the Anchor Structure and Hierarchy (Document 20) points out the law network is the causal base; if settings on the base are casually rewritten, it equals tearing up and rewriting the causal ledger, which Myriad Ranks&#39; causality cannot bear;</li><li><strong>Readers&#39;-rights argument</strong>: Myriad Ranks are the civilizational story&#39;s co-authors and co-characters; retconning is deceiving readers, and ending unfinished is abandoning characters;</li><li><strong>Infinite-origin argument</strong>: under Axiom 6, conflict need not be manufactured by &quot;villains suddenly growing strong,&quot; but may be supplied by &quot;new law nodes awaiting lighting&quot; — with conflict&#39;s source right, the motive for retconning is gone.</li></ul><h2 id="iii-execution-mechanism" tabindex="-1">III. Execution Mechanism <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-execution-mechanism" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Execution Mechanism&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>The Alaya Network maintains a &quot;setting version library&quot;; all setting changes go through version-number management, old versions are not deleted but archived;</li><li>New-old setting conflicts automatically trigger an &quot;interpretation work order,&quot; giving a unifying explanation within a time limit;</li><li>The civilizational-evolution roadmap is publicly deduced by the Anchor Council to the closed-loop node; &quot;take one step, see one step&quot; is not allowed;</li><li>Quest Domain simulation-retrospective does special drills on &quot;retcon-style setting collapse,&quot; letting cultivators intuitively see retconning&#39;s civilizational cost.</li></ul><h2 id="iv-consequences-of-violation" tabindex="-1">IV. Consequences of Violation <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-consequences-of-violation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Consequences of Violation&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Light</strong>: setting expression inconsistent front and back, issue a unifying interpretation within a time limit;</li><li><strong>Medium</strong>: unilaterally overturning anchored settings for plot convenience, relevant plots are voided, responsible persons recorded in the integrity archive;</li><li><strong>Heavy</strong>: abandoning Myriad Ranks via &quot;unfinished ending,&quot; prematurely terminating civilizational evolution, is betrayal of all Myriad Ranks, and the Anchor Council launches a forced continuation procedure.</li></ul><h2 id="v-supervising-subjects" tabindex="-1">V. Supervising Subjects <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-supervising-subjects" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Supervising Subjects&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision&#39;s setting-version library is the first layer; the Anchor Supervisory Committee checks &quot;retcon-style setting changes&quot; as the second layer; the Symbiotic Court adjudicates setting-tampering cases as the third layer; Myriad Ranks&#39; clans, as &quot;readers,&quot; have direct commentary and accountability over unfinished endings and retconning as the fourth layer.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: retconning and unfinished endings let immeasurable causal accumulation go to zero with voiding, civilizational-level waste</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: no retconning also refuses to launder old predation settings into new justice; under Axiom 6 everyone inherently possesses infinite origin, predation loses meaning</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo-type systems power up on a word and change settings on a whim, protagonist halo over everything; Heng Yuan Zhou settings are versioned, and even the strong cannot temporarily add scenes</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: the closed-loop ending is Myriad Ranks&#39; common ending, not one protagonist&#39;s private perfection</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: the worldview may expand infinitely (Rule 24), but every expansion goes through version management, no collapse, no unfinished</li></ul><p>Never retcon, never end unfinished has another layer of meaning for cultivators individually: it guarantees the cultivator&#39;s lifelong investment is not crossed out by the &quot;author.&quot; In the old cosmos, once the protagonist switches realm systems, predecessors&#39; arduous cultivation becomes a joke; in Heng Yuan Zhou, a cultivator&#39;s century of deduction, pits stepped in, and Dao texts left permanently enter the version library, becoming Myriad Ranks&#39; permanent wealth. No retconning is ultimately respect for every cultivator who cultivates seriously — your effort will not be betrayed by the plot.</p><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Never retcon, never end unfinished, is civilizational finalization&#39;s promise to &quot;completeness.&quot; Heng Yuan Zhou this great book must be written to the last line of Myriad Ranks&#39; joint ascension.</p><p>In the end, the Rule 21 described in this entry — never retcon, never end unfinished — is no isolated case; it consistently points to the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization&#39;s co-construction direction.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/20-锚点结构与层级.html">Entry 20 · Anchor Structure and Hierarchy</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/954_模块5-规则二十-法则先行.html">Entry 954 · Rule 20 The Law Comes First</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/956_模块5-规则二十二-设定自洽高于剧情便利.html">Entry 956 · Rule 22 Setting Self-Consistency Above Plot Convenience</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/958_模块5-规则二十四-世界观可无限扩容.html">Entry 958 · Rule 24 The Worldview May Expand Infinitely</a></li></ul>',23)])])}const m=n(a,[["render",r]]);export{g as __pageData,m as default};
